From: PvrGPU contributors
Subject: [PATCH] pco: preserve explicitly legalized native TCS/TES stages

Pinned Mesa 26.2.1 da14d65e4499e66468094be52bff9ea0915a695e.
Apply after mesa-26.2.1-pco-geometry-stage.patch. The caller lowers actual
per-vertex/per-patch IO to native LD/ST and TES exports to UVSW writes.
TCS ends a native task without an implicit vertex export; TES exports one
evaluated vertex. Stage identities remain TESS_CTRL/TESS_EVAL throughout.
The caller executes each bounded <=32 invocation TCS patch in one native
instruction-group-lockstep task, matching PCO's single-task barrier rule.

--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco.h
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco.h
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 /* Native Geometry stage with UVSW write/emit/cut/endtask.  The Gallium
  * caller owns explicit input-memory and output-slot layout legalization. */
 #define PCO_HAS_GEOMETRY_SHADER 1
+#define PCO_HAS_TESSELLATION_SHADERS 1
 
 pco_ctx *pco_ctx_create(const struct pvr_device_info *dev_info,
                         const struct pvr_device_runtime_info *dev_runtime_info,
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
@@ -418,6 +418,8 @@
       return gather_cs_data(nir, data);
 
    case MESA_SHADER_GEOMETRY:
+   case MESA_SHADER_TESS_CTRL:
+   case MESA_SHADER_TESS_EVAL:
       return;
 
    default:
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_end.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_end.c
@@ -32,7 +32,8 @@
    pco_builder b =
       pco_builder_create(entry, pco_cursor_after_block(last_block));
 
-   if (shader->stage == MESA_SHADER_VERTEX) {
+   if (shader->stage == MESA_SHADER_VERTEX ||
+       shader->stage == MESA_SHADER_TESS_EVAL) {
       if (last_instr && last_instr->op == PCO_OP_UVSW_WRITE &&
           pco_instr_has_default_exec(last_instr) &&
           pco_instr_get_rpt(last_instr) == 1) {
